_struct_biol.id                    1 
_struct_biol.details               
;THE ENZYME IS HEXADECAMER AND CONSISTS OF EIGHT LARGE AND
EIGHT SMALL SUBUNITS.  THE CHAINS ID'S OF LARGE SUBUNITS ARE
A,B,C,D,E,F,G AND H.  THE CHAINS ID'S OF SMALL SUBUNITS ARE
S,T,U,V,W,X,Y AND Z.  FOUR LARGE SUBUNITS (L) AND FOUR SMALL
SUBUNITS (S) ARE CONTAINED IN THE ASYMMETRIC UNIT.
A PAIR OF L4S4 UNITS RELATED BY THE CRYSTALLOGRAPHIC 2-FOLD
GENERATES THE HEXADECAMER.  CATALYTIC UNITS OF THE ENZYME AR
L2S2 WHICH IS CONSTITUTED BY CHAINS ABST, CDUV, EFWX AND GHY
OF THE HEXADECAMER.
;
_struct_biol.pdbx_parent_biol_id   ? 
